  "notes": "KANJI: Can be written as {転|こ}ける.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Intransitive.\n\nREGIONAL NOTE: More common in Western Japan (Kansai region). In Eastern Japan (Kanto), {転|ころ}ぶ is more common.\n\nCONJUGATION: Despite ending in -eru, this is an ichidan (vowel-stem) verb: こけない, こけます, こけて, etc.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {転|ころ}ぶ (to fall - more standard/Eastern)\n- {倒|たお}れる (to fall over, collapse - larger scale)",
